          "id": "D",
          "text": "A",
          "html": "A"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p>The difference we could see is the position of dots. The dots are on the same side of the square, even if the position of cube or triangle changes. But in Image (C), the position of dots is diagonally opposite.</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/08/F2_Savita_Defence_25-8-23_D23.png\" style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); width: 433px; height: 82px;\" /></p>\n",
